#! ia 1.0

@lane authority
  meaning
    says "The authority lane — where governance and authority-facet contracts land: the norms and authority-facet contracts that say what must hold. Derived from @kind governance and @kind contract (authority facet)."
    answers "Does the work need the obligations that govern it?"
  data
    order 0

@lane contracts
  meaning
    says "The contracts lane — where non-authority contracts land: the agreed shapes and interfaces records fill. Derived from @kind contract (non-authority facet)."
    answers "Does the work need the structures or agreements it must satisfy?"
  data
    order 1

@lane definitions
  meaning
    says "The definitions lane — where definitional nodes land: the declarations of what things ARE. Derived from @kind definition."
    answers "Does the work need what its terms, boundaries and methods mean?"
  data
    order 2

@lane templates
  meaning
    says "The templates lane — where reusable scaffolds land: the parameterized shapes instantiated into concrete records. Derived from @kind template."
    answers "Does the work need a reusable output shape to fill?"
  data
    order 3

@lane enforcement
  meaning
    says "The enforcement lane — where gates and access rules land: the checks and policies evaluated at a crossing. Derived from @kind check and @kind policy."
    answers "Does the work need the gates and permission or routing rules it will cross?"
  data
    order 4

@lane bindings
  meaning
    says "The bindings lane — where executable connections land: actors, invocations and triggers wired to behavior a host supplies. Derived from @kind binding."
    answers "Does the work need the actors, invocations or triggers wired to behavior?"
  data
    order 5

